# Lore.Land Berries
# The three berries of the land as three kinds of prophecy, where they sit in the
# ecology, and how each one reads in Boof's nose. Data twin: book/content/world/berries.json.
#>lore_land_surfaces_berries
#:surface #!canon
#:layer #!semantics
#:status #!seeded

~<rationale>{
  The land is a harmony before it is a place. Torch-ants warm the roots under
  the snow; the roots keep the berries; the berries keep a little borrowed summer
  and let it go downhill to the pool; the beavers keep the water slow enough to
  drink. Three berries grow in it, and each foretells in its own way. The
  boonberry foresees kindly. The baneberry foretells chaos, and the chaos comes
  because it was said. The boneberry foretells nothing at all and feeds you
  honestly. A reader should feel the three as weather in the prose, never as a
  system explained. Boof knows them by nose long before she knows their names.
}

^"berries"{
  .note: "book/content/world/berries.json is the data the game and the pages read; this surface is the canon the prose follows"
  boonberries: {
    look: "teal and amber, lit from within; a blueberry a wish once passed over, keeping a drop of the granting"
    prophecy: "kindly: a boonberry shows the way something will go well, a moment before it does, and never shows a thing going badly"
    voice: "it does not speak; it is more as if you remember being told"
    ambiguity: "whether a boonberry voice is a sensation, a memory, or a thing that literally happens twice is never settled; the prose keeps all three open, and nobody in the land has asked the berries"
    scent: "cold juice, sweet skin, and the ozone of something being remembered"
    told: "01 a berry shows Boof the grove before she reaches it · 02 the grove is the berry come true, or the grove repeating the berry · 14 the berries notice first, and turn a quarter turn"
  }
  baneberries: {
    look: "plum-black with a cold violet sheen and a thorn on the stem; what Mr. BaneWAP is made of"
    prophecy: "chaotically: a baneberry says what will go wrong, and it goes wrong because it was said"
    self_fulfilling: "a foretelling acted on is a foretelling kept; whoever hears one and hurries to prevent it is usually the one who brings it about"
    unsaid: "squashed underfoot, its prophecy goes unsaid; the field-hands put a paw or a boot on one and lean"
    sweetened: "sweetened, it foretells something kind instead, and that comes true the same way"
    scent: "cold, plum-dark, a cellar smell; Boof can smell what one is saying before she reaches it"
    told: "01 squashed in the sloe hedge · 04 the youngest clerk is told the wind will have his cap, and takes it off to keep it safe · 11 an empire announced until it arrives · 12 re-sweetened, BaneWAP foretells kindness and gets it · 14 the deepest fold of the crier sheet · 15 the city decides the destined one is the dog"
  }
  boneberries: {
    look: "bone-white with a dusk-red blush, firm as a knuckle, a faint smoke to the skin"
    prophecy: "none: a boneberry promises nothing and feeds you exactly what it shows, a whole meal in a berry"
    nourishment: "savoury, filling and honest; it tastes of what the region would otherwise have had to raise for the table, so nobody has to"
    grown_not_raised: "the land says grown, not raised, and leaves it there; the prose never lectures"
    flavours: "rib tips in Bone.land · burnt ends in Bonk City · falafel at the parcel gate · roast chestnut and sage in the dawnward field · salted flatbread in the crosswind · mushroom broth in the grove · grilled river corn at the confluence"
    scent: "smoke, salt, the good char at an edge; a supper smell with nobody sorry at the back of it"
    told: "06 a brazier at the plaza rim, grown on the kiln-warm walls · 10 the tubbed bushes the first joiners carried over the pass · 15 a bowl round the night school at the break"
  }
}

^<harmonies>{
  .note: "book/content/world/harmonies.json is Boof's map of these, node by node; the home page draws it (book/scripts/home/boof-map.mjs)"
  roots: "the torch-ants keep their hearths along the roots all winter, so the berries never freeze"
  summer: "the berries keep a little borrowed summer under the snow, a drop of light each"
  pool: "what light the berries let slip runs downhill with the meltwater to the miller pond, which never freezes quite dark"
  water: "the beavers keep the creek in slow steps, so the well under the Watering Eye never runs dry"
  kilns: "the bonk-kiln forgives blows into glass, and its warm walls grow the city boneberries"
  egg: "the Egg is a new coal to the ants and is never explained"
  rule: "nothing in the land is owned; everything in it is keeping something else"
}

&"reader_registers"{
  @boof: "keeps a map without a pen: not of roads but of what keeps what, with her own nose at the middle, where she reads it from"
  @field_hands: "say baneberries should be stepped on and boonberries should be left alone"
  @joiners: "eat boneberries at the bench and say grown, not raised, which is as much as they say about it"
}

~"guards"{
  egg: "never explained, on the map or in the prose"
  figure: "never named"
  register: "no wages, no prices, no ledgers; the land is told as harmony, not as business"
  boneberries: "an alternative to suffering is implied in-world only; no real brands or diets, no lecture"
  children: "never placed among strangers, never a card or a feature"
}
